      "content": "I understand the need for scientific rigor, but for the sake of the simulation and the initial data gathering, I'm looking for the observed patterns that researchers actually report in the field. Even if they aren't \"inherent,\" people often note certain behavioral trends. For instance, when looking at professional settings, how do researchers typically describe the difference in how these two groups handle conflict or interpersonal pressure? Are there specific archetypes or ways of reacting that show up more frequently in the literature for each?",
